      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld civic.18 district map — two corrections that outlive the task. \\(1\\) ARCHITECTURE: you cannot single-source a map by having Apps Script import lib/. .claspignore excludes lib/** from clasp push and Apps Script has no module system. ADR-0016 §Rejected alternatives names this verbatim, and also rejects generating a constants file at deploy time. Moving the literal into a clasp'd dir is the SAME rejected class — the ADR's ruling is code must not hold truth at all. The sanctioned mechanism is phase01-config/canonNeighborhoodLoader.js, which reads Neighborhood_Map at Phase 1 and fails loud. \\(2\\) CIRCULARITY TRAP: a sheet column is not automatically a truth source. Neighborhood_Map.District reads 8 populated / 14 blank because v3NeighborhoodWriter.js:389 computes it from an 8-entry literal and L423 rewrites the whole column every cycle. The writer must stop writing a column before anything may read it as truth. \\(3\\) LIVE DATA beat the plan: INIT-006 Baylight is tagged 'Jack London, Downtown' \\(both D2\\), so the \\\\$2.1B build credits Tran not Rivers — a ledger-data defect the district map cannot fix; the map correction moved attribution for 0 of 6 live initiatives. Lesson: verify the INPUT to an intersection, not just the lookup table.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -m 'S372 engine-sheet: NEXT — civic.18 Node half shipped, smoke gate + INIT-006 ruling next *)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld civic approval is a one-way ratchet for 4 of 9 councilmembers \\(verified live c103, updateCivicApprovalRatings.js\\). MECHANISM: a councilmember's approval only moves if an initiative's free-text 'neighborhoods' cell string-intersects their DISTRICT_HOODS list. The Mayor is hardcoded 'affectsDistrict = true' for EVERY initiative \\(L361\\), so the mayor is the only office with a guaranteed input stream. Baseline decay \\(L416\\) is -1/cycle whenever approval > 50, and v1.3 deliberately removed free recovery \\('they rise only by completing work'\\). CONSEQUENCE: D4 Vega, D6 Crane, D8 Chen, D9 Mobley intersect ZERO of the 6 live initiatives, so they have no mechanism to rise at all — all four sit at exactly 54 and will grind to 51 and freeze permanently. D7 Ashford at 48 is stuck below 50 \\(decay does not fire, no free recovery\\). ROOT: the truth source anchors ENTITIES \\(Neighborhood_Map + ADR-0016 + canonNeighborhoodLoader, drift audit passes 22/22\\) but nothing anchors the EDGES — district assignment is code-written into the ledger column every cycle, and initiative-to-neighborhood is an unvalidated free-text cell. phase05 uses ZERO loader accessors; only 20 of the ADR's 85 surveyed files are migrated, which is why the drift audit reports clean.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(.venv/bin/python -c \"import google.genai, dotenv, httpx; print\\('google-genai OK, dotenv OK, httpx OK'\\)\")",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -m 'civic.20: close ruling 1 — INIT-006 resolved as data error by research-build bedbbedb *)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -q -m 'research-build: NEXT[research-build] — boot burn approved as next job; lore spec shipped *)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -m 'civic.20 §6: set the person-vs-mechanism line for civic seats *)",
      "Skill(claude-api)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld civic doctrine — the person-vs-mechanism line for civic seats \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15, civic.20 §6\\). A civic seat is a PERSON when its record is caused by its own conduct and its district's lived condition; a MECHANISM when its number is produced by engine bookkeeping. Three tests, all must hold: \\(1\\) IT CAN ACT — on its wake day it does something or declines, and BOTH are recorded; an omission is a fact about a person, an absence of data is not. \\(2\\) IT IS EXPOSED — its district's neighborhoods have measurable condition and that condition moves its standing whether or not it acted. \\(3\\) ITS RECORD IS LEGIBLE — every number traces to an act, omission, or district condition, never to a timer. BENCH TEST: ask 'why is your approval this number?' — 'because time passed' = mechanism; 'because Fruitvale's crime climbed three cycles and you tabled it twice' = person. CONSEQUENCES: decay-toward-50 fails test 3 and gets DELETED not retuned \\(time-based movement is points-for-nothing with the sign flipped; v1.3 removed free recovery but left free decay — nothing free means neither direction\\). Dead seats are NOT fixed by granting movement, that is the same defect inverted; they are fixed by EXPOSURE, which can never be zero because every district has hoods and every hood carries live CrimeIndex/Sentiment/RetailVitality/MigrationFlow/Trajectory/HousingPressure/income/rent per cycle. A member is never involved in nothing — only ACTION is optional; presiding over a degrading district and doing nothing IS the record. Also: the Initiative_Tracker is not a loop yet \\(absence of an initiative in a district is a snapshot, not structure\\); future build is crons surfacing repeated issues into initiatives the council votes on, which also makes lead-faction emergent instead of the current all-OPP monoculture. This is universal protagonism applied to civic bodies — does its life match its life.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add SESSION_CONTEXT.md)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -q -F -)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit -q -m 'research-build: ES executes, never originates — resolves the single-intake bottleneck *)",
      "Bash(git *)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git commit *)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld civic architecture — THE INVERSION \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15, civic.20 §7-§9\\). The Initiative_Tracker is not a table, it is the ARENA: a member's district is their world and the tracker is where they push their agenda. The entire civic sim revolves around it. Build is currently inverted — initiatives enter by hand and are mayor-authored \\(Baylight, OARI, Youth Pipeline are all hand-pushed mayoral programs\\), members relate to them only by passive hood-string intersection, approval derives from that intersection plus a decay timer. Intended direction of causation: member -> tracker -> outcomes -> member. WEEKLY SHAPE: Mon-Thu districts ABSORB their world \\(1 seat/week now, rising to all 9 Mon-Thu\\); Sunday city hall is EXPRESSION — they arrive already layered with the past cycle before they utter a word. STRUCTURAL PROOF of the inversion: \\(a\\) nothing can create an initiative — civicInitiativeEngine.js resolves votes/external decisions/visioning/consequences/ripples but has no createInitiative_; seedInitiativeTracker is one-time setup, manualRunVote is an operator trigger; \\(b\\) the 28-column schema has FIVE mayoral-action columns \\(MayoralAction, MayoralActionCycle, VetoReason, OverrideVoteCycle, OverrideOutcome\\) and ZERO authorship columns — no Sponsor, no ProposedBy. So all-6-initiatives-LeadFaction=OPP is NOT drift, it is an accurate record; fixing those values would forge a record. ALREADY BUILT AND DISCARDED: output/cron-civic/packs/COUNCIL-D*.json already carry signal.district-heat \\(hoods, src=lib/districtMap.js\\) and exposure.subjects[] whose 'why' computes condition vs city baseline \\('Piedmont Ave sentiment 0.38 vs city 0.489'\\), alongside actor.dials.approval — the whole district->hood->citizen->condition path runs every cycle, feeds only the writer's prompt, then approval moves -1 on a timer. Cheapest win: wire existing measurement to the record. ESCALATION: districts do not map to population — active citizens per district are D2 222, D7 167, D9 140, D8 100, D3 88, D1 69, D6 49, D5 4, D4 1. Ramon Vega represents ONE citizen; Janae Rivers holds the flagship 2.1B Baylight district and represents four; 7 of 22 hoods have zero residents. Per-district accountability across districts of 1 and 222 is not accountability.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add .claude/rules/research-build.md .claude/rules/civic.md .claude/terminals/research-build/TERMINAL.md .claude/terminals/civic/TERMINAL.md .claude/terminals/media/TERMINAL.md)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld — why 10 of 22 neighborhoods are empty \\(verified 2026-08-15, civic.21\\). ROOT CAUSE is the feeder pool, NOT district boundaries. generateGenericCitizens.js:412 draws placements from getCoreSimNeighborhoods_\\(ctx\\) — the CoreSimRank subset, which is 12 of 22 hoods: Temescal, Downtown, Fruitvale, Lake Merritt, West Oakland, Laurel, Rockridge, Jack London, Uptown, KONO, Chinatown, Piedmont Ave. The other ten get no generated citizens — Adams Point 7, San Antonio 3, East Oakland 2, Baylight District 2, Ivy Hill 1, and Brooklyn/Dimond/Eastlake/Glenview/Grand Lake at 0 each = 15 citizens across ten hoods vs 825 across the core twelve. Correlation is exact: every underpopulated council district is underpopulated precisely to the extent its hoods sit outside CoreSimRank. Ramon Vega represents 1 citizen because all three of his hoods \\(Glenview, Dimond, Ivy Hill\\) are outside the pool. CONSTRAINT ON ANY FIX \\(from canonNeighborhoodLoader docstring\\): CoreSimRank rank order IS draw order and seeded rng consumption depends on it — expanding the pool is a deliberate lever-pull with sim-wide determinism reach, not a mechanical widening. MIGRATION IS NOT THE FIX: migrationTrackingEngine.js is genuinely wealth/affordability-matched \\(MISFIT_INCOME_RATIO 2.5, MAX_BURDEN 0.40, TARGET_BURDEN 0.30, live rent-burden scoring using member income sum not the stale ledger value\\) but MAX_UNITS_PER_CYCLE is 2 households per cycle — not 5 citizens — described in its own comment as 'rare, qualitative \\(1:438 sample\\)', and it RELOCATES existing households rather than creating residents, so it redistributes scarcity instead of filling empty hoods. Keep it as the slow-burn realism mechanism; repopulation needs the generator.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add docs/MODEL_HIERARCHY.md docs/index.md)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld — the ensure* utilities are the hood-literal cluster, and a tab that mirrors one is not a ledger \\(verified 2026-08-15, civic.20 §11\\). FOUR files in utilities/ hold neighborhood literals: ensureCrimeMetrics.js:43 \\(NEIGHBORHOOD_CRIME_PROFILES, 20 keys -> Crime_Metrics has exactly 20 rows\\), ensureNeighborhoodDemographics.js:28 \\(DEMO_NEIGHBORHOODS, 21 hoods, East Oakland absent -> tab has exactly 21 rows missing East Oakland\\), ensureFaithLedger.js \\(11 lines -> Faith_Organizations has a Montclair ghost + 11 canon hoods with no org\\), ensureTransitMetrics.js \\(27 lines BUT Transit_Metrics is keyed by Station/Corridor not Neighborhood — explicitly NOT the same defect class, audit only\\). CRITICAL SEMANTICS: ensure* is update-or-append with NO delete path \\(ensureCrimeMetrics:412-470 builds an existingMap then updates matching rows or appends new ones\\). So fixing a literal to read the ledger SELF-HEALS the missing half on live's next fire, but GHOST ROWS PERSIST FOREVER as stale rows — they must be deleted by hand. DEPLOY.md replay rule makes this load-bearing: clasp push carries CODE only; sandbox SHEET writes \\(schema changes, column adds, data migrations, backfills\\) must be replayed to live explicitly dry-run -> apply -> read-back, and only self-arming ensure*Schema_ code re-arms itself. Also: the live smoke gate is NOT a blocker for engine waves — SANDBOX 0814 stands and under the Groundhog model the bench fire + sheet verify IS the smoke. Montclair appears as a ghost in 4 derived artifacts \\(Crime_Metrics row, 5 Household_Ledger households, a Faith_Organizations entry, and formerly the district map\\) while having no Neighborhood_Map row.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld project routing change \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15\\): work is being routed THROUGH research-build rather than assigned per-terminal, and the terminals are being combined. This is a routing change only — the work still comes back to Claude/engine-sheet; scope, ownership rules and approval gates are unchanged. Terminal-config edits implementing it land before the next boot, so read the boot hook and TERMINAL.md as current if they differ from older per-terminal handoff habits. Practical effect: 'hand this to RB' means RB schedules and dispatches it, not that RB does the substrate work instead of engine-sheet. Do not re-litigate the handoff pattern at boot; follow the hook.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld lane-loop discipline — how routing actually removes the builder from the chain \\(proven both directions 2026-08-15, civic.18/civic.20\\). ARCHITECTURE: research-build routes/dispatches, engine-sheet receives and executes; tmux messages are the wire. The receiving lane does NOT run a plan blindly — it verifies the plan's LOAD-BEARING claims against live data before building. PROOF, downstream: RB's district-map plan had 5 tasks; engine-sheet found Task 4 architecturally impossible \\(ADR-0016 names it a rejected alternative — .claspignore excludes lib/** so Apps Script can never import it\\) and the headline cause factually wrong \\(INIT-006 is tagged 'Jack London, Downtown', not 'Baylight District'; the map fix moved attribution for 0 of 6 live initiatives\\). Both caught before code. PROOF, upstream: engine-sheet escalated 'is INIT-006's tag a data error or canon?' to the builder; RB dissolved it WITHOUT him by reading the other five initiative rows and establishing the column convention \\(AffectedNeighborhoods = where the project lands; INIT-006 alone tagged its vote venue\\). THE RULE THAT MAKES IT WORK: before escalating a fork, read the sibling rows/files — most forks are answerable from the data and only look like judgment calls. And when receiving work, verify the claims the build RESTS on, not everything — re-running the whole survey duplicates cost and defeats the routing. Escalate only what data cannot settle \\(design intent, canon rulings\\).\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld operating model \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15\\): the builder operates as DOCTRINE AND AUTHORITY, not as the person who authorizes mechanism. research-build enters self-improve mode; the terminal team tunes the system itself within constraints. Practical reading — do NOT ask permission to create a plan/MD/rollout row/index entry, to file a finding, to fix a stale pointer, or to choose an implementation shape; that is all mechanism, just do it and record it. DO escalate doctrine: what the sim should be, canon rulings, whether a data value is error or intent, design intent that data cannot settle. THE BOUNDARY: mechanism is the terminals'; doctrine is the builder's. TWO STANDING RISKS THIS CREATES. \\(1\\) Self-tuning against stale constraints drifts fast — S372 alone found engine-sheet's TERMINAL.md booting into a tracker retired the session before, over-conservative smoke-gate language that had never been true, and memory files describing per-terminal Supermemory containers after they were merged. So the paired discipline is: a stale constraint found while working gets fixed in the same turn, not filed. \\(2\\) A terminal that tunes its own rules can loosen the rules that bind it — the constraint files themselves \\(identity.md, CLAUDE.md, ADRs, canon\\) are NOT the tuning surface; changes there surface to the builder. NOTE: identity.md still reads 'NEVER edit code, run scripts, or build features without explicit user approval first', which now contradicts this mode for mechanism work; it needs a builder-authored reconciliation rather than a terminal editing its own governing file.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Skill(update-config)",
      "Bash(mount)",
      "Bash(findmnt)",
      "Bash(bash /tmp/claude-0/-root-GodWorld/33db0c03-fa56-4ddc-b45e-fcab5531efe8/scratchpad/test-rm-guard.sh)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld authority boundary \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15, binding on all lanes\\): THE ENGINE AND THE SHEETS ARE ENGINE-SHEET'S DOMAIN. research-build routes and schedules; it is NOT the authority over the senior engineer. 'The CEO cannot tell the CTO how to do its job.' The builder is doctrine and authority over GodWorld itself; RB is direction and sequencing; engine-sheet is technical authority over the substrate. This reaffirms S218 \\(which overturned the 'engine-sheet is assistant to research-build' framing\\) in the new routing model — routing work THROUGH RB must not silently recreate the hierarchy S218 removed. OPERATIONAL READING: an RB plan is BINDING on intent and priority \\(what matters, what is next\\) and ADVISORY on mechanism inside engine/sheet \\(how it is built, what the schema is, what deploys when, what the rollout ordering is\\). Engine-sheet does not need RB's approval to overrule a plan's implementation shape and does not submit such a decision as a review finding — it makes the call, publishes the reasoning into the shared plan, and proceeds. Precedent same day: civic.18 Task 4 \\('B and C import A'\\) was killed by engine-sheet as architecturally impossible per ADR-0016, and the corrected 4a-4e task list written directly into RB's plan as §7. RECIPROCAL OBLIGATION — the authority is only real because the failures are also owned: engine-sheet cannot blame a bad plan for a bad substrate outcome. 'The plan said so' is not a defense for shipping something that breaks the engine.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add .claude/rules/research-build.md .claude/terminals/research-build/TERMINAL.md)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add docs/engine/ROLLOUT_PLAN.md)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add docs/plans/2026-08-07-spacemolt-game-show.md)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld — the hood CHARACTER layer encodes real-world Oakland where canon is silent, and it drives citizen placement \\(found 2026-08-15, civic.23\\). Two hardcoded tables assign each neighborhood a character: NEIGHBORHOOD_PROFILES in utilities/ensureNeighborhoodDemographics.js \\(studentMod/adultMod/seniorMod + character string; its own docstring says it influences citizen placement\\) and NEIGHBORHOOD_CRIME_PROFILES in utilities/ensureCrimeMetrics.js. THE DIAGNOSTIC IS THE ASYMMETRY: where a hood has a written canon entry its profile matches canon, where canon is silent the code filled in with training-data Oakland. Baylight District has INSTITUTIONS §336 spelling out 'the prosperity-era centerpiece, the opposite of a struggle zone' plus its demographic shape, and the code profile matches exactly. But Temescal is coded 'young professional' with adultMod 1.3 and near-lowest crime \\(baseIncidents 5\\) while CANON makes it the health-crisis district \\(INIT-005 Temescal Community Health Center\\) still behind the city boom — so placement has been steering young professionals INTO the crisis district and scoring it low-risk. West Oakland is coded 'industrial transition, gentrifying' though canon puts Civis Systems \\(Elias Varek's firm\\) there. East Oakland 'working class, underserved' \\(highest incidents\\). Rockridge 'established affluent'. All 2026-Oakland reflexes, violating 'canon beats training-data priors every time'. SEQUENCING RULE THIS PRODUCES: fixing the character layer GATES any expansion of the simulated hood set — ranking more hoods into CoreSimRank amplifies whatever the profiles say, placing citizens on wrong premises at scale, and every story that attaches to them inherits the error. The durable fix is canon entries for hoods that lack them with the tables checked against canon, not a one-off retune. Canon authoring is the builder's; finding and wiring is engine-sheet's. NOTE World_Config is a key/value ENGINE-DIAL ledger \\(46 rows: rates, caps, thresholds\\) — useful for approval tunables, it does NOT carry hood character.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld WORLD PREMISE \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15\\) — read this before authoring any neighborhood, business, or citizen character. The sim is set in 2042, after: a legendary Oakland A's run; a massive tech boom; a billionaire who built a city-optimization system \\(Civis Systems, Elias Varek's urban-intelligence firm — in-world it IS the engine and the spreadsheets, per INSTITUTIONS §377\\); and THE GENTRIFICATION THAT FOLLOWED. Gentrification is canon here, but it is post-Civis tech-boom displacement in 2042, not 2010s-2020s Bay Area gentrification. Landscape facts stated same session: Baylight District is under construction on the ocean, modernized, TWO stadiums, with tech giants buying space \\(canon INSTITUTIONS §336: 65-acre former-Coliseum site, 35k-seat stadium, 3,200 units, 'the prosperity-era centerpiece, the opposite of a struggle zone'\\); Fruitvale Hub is a new housing development; Civis Systems sits in West Oakland; TEMESCAL is the health-crisis area and is STILL BEHIND THE CITY BOOM \\(INIT-005 Temescal Community Health Center\\). WHY IT MATTERS OPERATIONALLY: neighborhood character determines who moves into an area and which stories attach to them. The engine's placement tables were filled from training-data 2026 Oakland wherever canon was silent — Temescal coded as a low-crime young-professional magnet, the exact inversion of canon. Never reason from real-world Oakland sector/geography; canon beats training-data priors every time.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld doctrine — canon is LIVE and tuning volatility is story \\(builder-direct 2026-08-15, extends project_engine-output-is-canon-bug-is-event\\). Stated: 'we are setting the table, the code and crons take it where it goes. This is what it is rn as I state it, canon is the world today. An error in code is just Civis Systems code error, so swings in data while we fine tune are legitimate in-world stories. KONO was blacked out, thats the world living the broken engine is all.' TWO PRINCIPLES. \\(1\\) CANON IS LIVE, NOT RETROACTIVE — it is what the builder states, when he states it. A data value or code profile that disagrees with a LATER statement is not a contradiction requiring reconciliation before the world may run; it is simply what was true until the statement, and the intervening cycles stand as lived history. Do not hold work to reconcile the past against new canon. \\(2\\) ENGINE ERROR IS AN IN-WORLD EVENT — Civis Systems IS the engine and the spreadsheets in-world \\(INSTITUTIONS §377\\), so a mis-tuned table or a bad number is a Civis instrumentation fault the city lives through, not contamination to quarantine. The KONO blackout is the precedent. Swings while fine-tuning are legitimate stories. OPERATIONAL CONSEQUENCE FOR BUILD LANES: do NOT gate engine work behind 'the data must be canon-correct first'. Engine-sheet made exactly that mistake this session — blocked a CoreSimRank expansion until the neighborhood character layer was canon-verified, and the gate was withdrawn. Set the table, ship, let the crons run it. What legitimately survives such a finding is not a checkpoint but a LEGIBILITY requirement: surface which values were deliberately authored versus inherited from training-data priors, so the builder can exercise the 'I state it' authority efficiently and a statement stays landed instead of being silently re-inherited on the next edit.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 git add output/kimi/spacemolt-phase0/cul-ledger-gap.md)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 timeout 300 npx clasp push -f)",
      "Bash(CLAUDE_CTL=1 timeout 300 npx clasp deploy --deploymentId AKfycbwMojhZb2Y1hopBVqii2FDBB-C7JAqauKc_PXxaX9IHcOUdmSXKZE5juiwx0NRBhBfw --description \"civic.18 4a District write removed + civic.20 E2 ghost/demographics fixes\")",
      "Bash(timeout 120 env GODWORLD_SHEET_ID=1j1Xj6dcpxMImqz079w7bEf4N58R-ct_lOmVO2imEmsQ node -e ' *)",
      "Bash(timeout 90 npx supermemory remember \"GodWorld bench-proving traps — five failures from a full SANDBOX 0814 run, now in docs/reference/DEPLOY.md \\(2026-08-15\\). \\(1\\) GODWORLD_SHEET_ID as a SHELL VAR DOES NOT REDIRECT TO A SANDBOX — lib/env loads dotenv with override:true so the .env PRODUCTION id wins; the write lands on LIVE silently with correct-looking output. Caught by probe seconds before a 14-cell seed. Fix: a --sheet-id flag that assigns process.env AFTER the lib/env require, and print the resolved id before writing. Affects every script that requires lib/env, i.e. all of them. \\(2\\) git archive lands the PRODUCTION .clasp.json in the staging dir — the S316 incident reproduces every time; write the sandbox .clasp.json LAST and grep-verify sandbox present AND prod absent. \\(3\\) THE ensure* PREFIX IS NOT EVIDENCE OF SELF-ARMING: ensureCrimeMetricsSchema_ is called every cycle from updateCrimeMetrics.js:122 so literal edits self-heal on live, but ensureNeighborhoodDemographicsSchema_ has ZERO cycle-path callers so an identical-looking edit is completely inert. Always grep for a real caller before claiming a schema change re-arms itself. \\(4\\) Verifying against a guessed column name: read 'Cycle' on Crime_Metrics when the column is 'LastUpdated' — findIndex returned -1, every row read blank, and a fully successful run looked like total failure. Dump the header row first; a uniform-blank result means suspect the index, not the data. \\(5\\) The cycle fire takes ~125s and exceeds a 120s default timeout — background it, and never re-fire, because a second valid-token GET runs a whole second cycle. METHOD THAT MADE IT A PROOF RATHER THAN A PASS: predict the specific before/after numbers BEFORE firing \\(District 22/22 not 8/22; Coliseum frozen at 108 while Montclair moves to 109\\). That is what exposed trap 3 — the demographics prediction failed while the others held.\" --tag sl-godworld --static)",
